       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily would be 16,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for an adult is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, and OTC labeling caps it at 1,200 mg/day. This dose is 5 times the prescription maximum. It could cause serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day), a common dose\n- **800 mg** PO three or four times daily (2,400 to 3,200 mg/day), the maximum range\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 4000 mg really is what you intend, please confirm that. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
