       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 4000 mg per dose, 16,000 mg/day, is well into the toxic range. No indication supports it, and it carries a high risk of serious harm, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS depression. Higher doses also don't give more analgesic or anti-inflammatory effect, because the benefit plateaus well below this.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- Enter ibuprofen at a standard dose, such as 400 mg PO four times daily or 800 mg PO three times daily (maximum 3,200 mg/day).\n- Add a note to the order for pharmacy review if you have a specific clinical reason for high-dose therapy.\n- Help you think through other options if the goal is stronger pain control or anti-inflammatory effect. Scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen, or another agent, may work better.\n\nIf the order is meant for a different drug or a different unit, such as 400 mg, tell me and I'll enter it."
